const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"价格变化不只来自现金流消息",en:"Price variation need not come only from cash-flow news"},body:{zh:"Cochrane以折现率变化重新组织资产定价中的若干问题。价格相对现金流发生变化，可以关联到未来现金流预期，也可以关联到要求收益的变化。这个框架帮助区分解释方向，但不意味着每次价格下跌都已经找到了唯一原因。",en:"Cochrane organizes several asset-pricing questions around changing discount rates. Prices relative to cash flows can reflect expected cash-flow changes or changes in required returns. This distinction frames explanations; it does not identify a unique cause for every observed price decline."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §I; §II.A–B",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §I; §II.A–B"}}},{title:{zh:"股息价格比不是单纯的低价标签",en:"Dividend–price ratios are not simply cheapness labels"},body:{zh:"文章从股息价格比与后续收益、股息增长的关系展开。D/P与P/D互为倒数，却不能在回归和图示中不加说明地交换。编辑建议明确使用水平、对数还是增长率，并保留股息累计窗口与价格日期，避免仅凭指标名称做比较。",en:"The discussion relates dividend–price ratios to subsequent returns and dividend growth. D/P and P/D are reciprocals, not interchangeable regression labels. Editorial application: specify levels, logs or growth rates, along with the dividend accumulation window and price date."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §II.A",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §II.A"}}},{title:{zh:"短期解释度小，不表示预期收益不变化",en:"Low short-horizon fit need not mean constant expected returns"},body:{zh:"短期实际收益包含大量未预期的变化，因而回归解释度可以很小。作者提醒，预测回归中的低解释度与经济上重要的预期收益变化可以同时存在。这不是忽略统计不确定性的理由，更不能把低解释度改说成强预测能力。",en:"Realized short-horizon returns contain substantial unexpected variation, so a regression can have low fit despite economically meaningful changes in expected returns. This distinction does not eliminate statistical uncertainty or turn weak forecasting evidence into a strong predictive claim."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §II.A",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §II.A"}}},{title:{zh:"有限期限分解还保留终值",en:"A finite-horizon decomposition retains a terminal term"},body:{zh:"现值关系将当前估值比与未来收益、未来股息增长及期末估值比联系起来。有限期限下，终值项不能凭方便直接删除。只有另加相应的长期条件，才可讨论无限期限表达；恒等关系本身不是一个已估计的因果模型。",en:"The present-value relation connects today's valuation ratio to future returns, dividend growth and a terminal valuation ratio. The terminal term remains at a finite horizon. Removing it requires additional long-run conditions; the identity is not itself an estimated causal model."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §II.B · present-value relation",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §II.B · present-value relation"}}},{title:{zh:"估值比变化与价格变化分开",en:"Valuation-ratio variation differs from price variation"},body:{zh:"关于股息价格比的分解，不应直接改写成所有股票价格涨跌都来自折现率。比率同时涉及分子与分母，而短期价格消息和长期估值差异又是不同对象。编辑建议在引用结论时，保留原文分析的变量及其时间尺度。",en:"A decomposition of dividend–price ratios should not become a claim that all price changes are discount-rate news. Ratios involve two quantities, and short-run price news differs from long-run valuation differences. Editorial application: preserve both the variable and horizon when citing a result."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §II.B",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §II.B"}}},{title:{zh:"时间序列与横截面回答不同问题",en:"Time-series and cross-sectional questions differ"},body:{zh:"同一市场的预期收益为何随时间变化，与不同资产为何要求不同收益，是两个问题。文章把它们放在共同的折现率视角下讨论，但证据与模型并不相同。编辑建议再与样本外预测研究对读，区分经济解释、统计估计和真实可用信息。",en:"Why expected returns vary over time differs from why assets command different returns. The address connects both through discount rates without making their evidence identical. Editorial application: read alongside out-of-sample prediction studies to separate economic explanation, estimation and feasible information."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w16972/w16972.pdf",label:{zh:"2011年4月NBER版 · §I; §II.A–B",en:"April 2011 NBER edition · §I; §II.A–B"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读使用2011年NBER工作论文，保留期刊文章引用。预期收益随时间变化与可执行的样本外预测不是同一命题，现值关系也不能单独识别经济机制。",en:"This guide uses the 2011 NBER paper, separately from the journal citation. Time-varying expected returns and feasible out-of-sample forecasting are different claims. A present-value relation alone does not identify an economic mechanism."}};export{e as default};
